From: Octagon SF8008 port
Subject: [PATCH] gfbdc: present the page that was just rendered

The flip opcode swaps surface and surface_back, so once the swap has
been done surface_back is the page that has just been rendered into and
surface is the page the next frame will be drawn to. The display has to
be panned to surface_back, but the code picks the opposite page: when
the new drawing target is the higher of the two it pans to the second
page, and otherwise back to the first one.

The result is that the contents of a frame only become visible one flip
later, and on a framebuffer whose page height differs from the height of
the scanout the image is left sitting at the wrong offset altogether.

Use getSurfaceOffset() on the finished surface instead. It computes the
offset from the physical address, so it stays correct no matter which
page the renderer started on, and returns 0 for an unallocated surface.

Upstream-Status: Pending
--- a/lib/gdi/gfbdc.cpp
+++ b/lib/gdi/gfbdc.cpp
@@ -195,10 +195,7 @@
 			surface = surface_back;
 			surface_back = s;
 
-			if (surface.data_phys > surface_back.data_phys)
-				fb->setOffset(surface_back.y);
-			else
-				fb->setOffset(0);
+			fb->setOffset(getSurfaceOffset(surface_back));
 		}
 #endif
 		break;
